# Groups finder

Say which kind of group is being searched, because Home Assistant areas, labels and light groups overlap. For example, a search for “Kitchen” may match an area, a label and a light group, and each means something different. Take membership from configuration, never from a matching name. Scope, result count, empty states, focus and the no-JavaScript fallback follow the [shared finder behaviour](../finder.html#finder-shared-contract).

## When to use it

Use it for explicitly configured household groups such as areas, labels or light groups. Membership can overlap, so name the kind of group being searched.

## Home Assistant boundary

A matching friendly name does not prove membership. This reference does not create areas, relabel entities or combine devices into a service target.

